{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1190836-1920-s-chicago-mage-game","id":1190836,"title":"1920's Chicago Mage Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-01T16:14:22-08:00","id":1190836,"title":"1920's Chicago Mage Game","content":"So, currently I'm writing up a Mage chronicle set in Chicago during the Prohibition era. I figured I'd come here to ask about any resources people might suggest beyond Wikipedia (for the prohibition era stuff), and if there are any Mage books I could buy that might have some information about Awakened society at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:20:43-08:00","id":1190840,"title":"","content":"Mage Noir technically takes place after WWII, but I can see a lot of material in it that would still be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T17:26:04-08:00","id":1190857,"title":"","content":"There's also a setting book for Chicago which is set in the modern era, but that you might be able to mine for some ideas. Apparently there's a giant treasure hunt for something called the Celestial Flange that's been going on for a long time there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T00:10:52-08:00","id":1191560,"title":"","content":"Good video if you want to run in Prohibition Era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, 'Fantastic Beasts and How to Find Them' could be good movie for inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ynk6uD78tI\" data-code=\"1ynk6uD78tI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1ynk6uD78tI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2018, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T20:06:17-08:00","id":1191818,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing everyone should read happens to be tangentially related:<br /> <a href=\"https://miltonfriedman.hoover.org/objects/57294/the-war-we-are-losing?ctx=5e5afe9e-d55f-42f3-bf47-598ec51e1f12&amp;idx=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://miltonfriedman.hoover.org/ob...c51e1f12&amp;idx=0</a><br /> <br /> Quite a few articles exist, and a skimmed a couple. The best I spotted was this: <a href=\"http://www.umich.edu/~eng217/student_projects/nkazmers/prohibition1.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.umich.edu/~eng217/student...hibition1.html</a><br /> <br /> <br /> As to specific books, well I can't think of any. I know I've read some from the era, but nothing leaps to my noggn. <i>The Great Gatsby</i> might be of some use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T11:53:26-08:00","id":1192335,"title":"","content":"I ran a Mage game set in the 20s. I made use of the 1920s investigator manual for Call of Cthulhu rpg. Also I think I found some Sears catalogues online somewhere from that decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:44:59-08:00","id":1193178,"title":"","con